{"name":"Football Pitch","hex":"#528e39","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"football pitch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A playing field on which the game of football is played.","An informal unit of measure of area, equal to the area of an Association football pitch (typically 76,900 square feet or 1.76 acres)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/football_pitch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Football pitch","blocks":[{"text":"A football pitch or soccer field is the playing surface for the game of association football. Its dimensions and markings are defined by Law 1 of the Laws of the Game, \"The Field of Play\". The pitch is typically made of natural turf or artificial turf, although amateur and recreational teams often play on dirt fields. Artificial surfaces are allowed only to be green in colour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Association_Football_field_diagram_-en.svg/330px-Association_Football_field_diagram_-en.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Football_pitch"},{"title":"Pitch (sports field)","blocks":[{"text":"A pitch or a sports ground is an outdoor playing area for various sports. The term pitch is most commonly used in British English, while the comparable term in Australian, American and Canadian English is playing field or sports field."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pitch_(sports_field)"},{"title":"Football","blocks":[{"text":"Football is a family of team sports in which the object is to get the ball over a goal line, into a goal, or between goalposts using merely the body."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Stoppage_in_an_AFL_game.jpg/330px-Stoppage_in_an_AFL_game.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Football"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo